Review:
Some of you hate-read reviews, so before you start crying about this '4 Star' review, go read the 8, 9 and 10 star reviews I gave to better comic book adaptations and comic character-themed films. This film receives a low score because of bad story telling. On paper, this movie sucks. Sure, the CONCEPT was great - sad origin story of the Joker. But, the application of that concept lead to a terrible script and bad film-making.At the end of the day, a comic book movie is entertainment and needs to be enjoyable - not just artistic. No one, and I mean NO ONE actually 'enjoyed' watching this film. Fail.RealReview Posting Scoring Criteria:
Acting: 1/1;
Casting: 1/1;
Directing: 1/1;
Story: 0.5/1;
Writing/Screenplay: 0/1;Total Base Score = 3.5Modifiers (+ or -):
Standout Performances: +1 ( Joaquin Phoenix - great Joker portrayal in a terrible movie);Tasteless Emotional Manipulation of Audience: -1 (9th grade writing 110, Week 2, Lesson #3: Everything is relative. It takes good to make bad. So, terrible event after terrible event just desensitizes the audience and bores people. I can't believe how bad the writing is in a film with a budget over $50 million);Total RealReview Rating: 3.5 (reluctantly rounded up to 4 for IMDB)

A loser in life, a joke in people's eyes, always ignored, never have a sense of existence.Passers-by bullied him, colleagues betrayed him, the host laughed at him...
No one cares about him. They treat him like nothing.He never knew if he really existed, and his only wish was that his death was worth more than his life.He was no clown, they said he was a useless clown;
He was really ill, and people expected him to pretend he wasn't.So he decided that he would no longer be a passer-by in other people's lives, he would be the master of his own.You call me a clown, I'll show you a clown.He who betrays me, I will show him what will happen to him.Whoever regards me as a joke, I will make him laugh no more.Once he wore a mask and always wanted to make others laugh.Now he has shed his disguise and just wants to live his life.He was a failure in one's eyes and a hero in another's.He danced on the world stage like an artist.He had thought of his life as a tragedy; now he realized that it was a comedy.
